# Line endings.
#
# Text is stored as LF in the repository whatever the machine's core.autocrlf is, so a tree cloned
# on Windows and a tree cloned on Linux produce the same commits and the same diffs. Without this
# every file in a Windows-authored repository arrives with CRLF and the first commit made from
# another machine rewrites the whole tree.
* text=auto

# Windows scripts keep native line endings on checkout.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Assets and archives the text filters must never touch.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.gif binary
*.ttf binary
*.jar binary
*.jks binary
*.keystore binary
*.apk binary
